				"rationale": "hat … in Anspruch genommen is one occurrence of the Collocation in Anspruch nehmen: nehmen only supports Anspruch (de/funktionsverbgefuege-are-collocations), and the perfect auxiliary hat joins the verbal unit (de/auxiliary-joins-the-verb-it-serves). Hilfe is its free accusative. The Reading is Duden's sense 1, 'make use of, avail oneself of' (jemanden beanspruchen, von etwas Gebrauch machen). It is 🤲, the taking emoji of nehmen, relabelled from 🙋, which read as volunteering (user ruling R5, 2026-10-03; label decided by agents under the user's delegation). Knowledge (#884): Nom S · Acc E (Duden jemanden, etwas in Anspruch nehmen; no E-VALBU entry); the noun's own auf belongs to the claim sense, so R4 adds no Slot. nutzen and wahrnehmen are near-synonyms: OpenThesaurus lists them for etwas in Anspruch nehmen, but they don't fit jemanden in Anspruch nehmen, and a relation holds for the whole Reading. Decided by agents under the user's delegation. beanspruchen is dropped: OpenThesaurus lists it only as (jemanden) beanspruchen beside behelligen and bemühen, and otherwise only Duden's gloss backs it (user, 2026-10-03, on the judges' split; R3)."
